Modifications: the four upstream skills were merged into one skill. The trace-collection workflow became a tool-choice matrix in SKILL.md and a per-symptom recipe file (references/symptoms.md); the two dotnet-trace references were merged; the dump skill's quick paths moved into SKILL.md and its references were trimmed; the Android and Apple symbolication skills were merged into references/mobile-symbolication.md with the logic of the Symbolicate-Tombstone.ps1 and Symbolicate-Crash.ps1 scripts restated as sed, jq, curl, llvm-symbolizer and atos commands (the scripts are not included); clr-activation-debugging was not ported. A dotnet-counters reference was written new from Microsoft Learn. All downloads were rewritten as download-to-file, inspect, then run, and every step that changes a production system now requires the user's go-ahead. PowerShell was kept only for Windows-only tools (PerfView, WER, procdump). Facts were rechecked against Microsoft Learn and the dotnet-monitor repository in October 2026, with these corrections: dotnet-trace --duration uses dd:hh:mm:ss; collect-linux needs glibc 2.27+ (not 2.35) and is a preview verb; DOTNET_DbgCreateDumpToolPath is a directory and applies to NativeAOT only; the default DOTNET_DbgMiniDumpType is 2 (Heap); dotnet-dump also supports Triage; dotnet-monitor trace profiles are Cpu, Http, Logs, Metrics and GcCollect (upstream used an invalid gc-verbose profile) and its sidecar example now uses listen mode, API key auth from a mounted Secret and image tag 10; perfcollect container capabilities are PERFMON and SYS_PTRACE before SYS_ADMIN, with DOTNET_ instead of COMPlus_ variables and the -nolttng note for LTTng 2.13+. Upstream eval notes, frontmatter routing text and cross-skill references were removed.
